okay so I have to confess something when  I first saw the iPhone six-plus I  thought it was kind of bonkers I mean I  get it people seem to really want larger  phones these days and Apple doesn't want  to leave any money on the table but have  you seen this thing I mean look this is  the 6 plus here's the iPhone 6 Batman  little boy that size is due to a display  that is larger than anything that's ever  appeared in an iPhone before but such a  honkin big screen makes for well kind of  an unwieldy phone I mean even with  Apple's clever reach ability screen  shrinking feature the iPhone 6 plus can  be kind of hard to handle if you don't  have giant NBA sized hands pocket  ability is another issue at 71  millimeters thick the iPhone 6 plus is  thin enough to fit into your pocket kind  of if you're into that sort of thing but  don't try sitting on and unless you like  the feeling of a 2x4 strapped to your  behind  so there's your newsflash larger things  are more cumbersome than smaller things  so those were my first impressions and I  do stand by them but there is I  discovered a different way to think  about the iPhone 6 plus and that started  happening when I used it like I used my  regular iPhone watching videos replying  to emails reading things off the web  man that bigger screen is nice with some  apps the iPhone 6 plus has different and  useful viewing modes when you turn it on  its side emails and messages take on a  more efficient layout and expanded  keyboard has dedicated keys for  copy/paste  and cursor movement videos are more fun  to watch and I certainly appreciated  reading on a large bright screen such as  this a larger size also means a larger  battery the iPhone 6 plus can do 12  hours of LTE browsing or 16 days of  standby time here's another thing about  the iPhone 6 plus it has the best camera  Apple has ever made that means it can  focus fast  a DSLR and shoot super slow-mo video but  it's also the first iPhone with optical  image stabilization that means that the  lens actually moves around within the  device to counter any shake that you  might create while holding it the result  is better low-light performance and  smoother video so what's the verdict  here it's tricky in some ways the issues  are more philosophical than  technological if we think of the iPhone  six-plus as a phone then it does seem  sort of large and clunky the standard  iPhone 6 does many of the same things in  a much smaller more convenient package  but maybe phone is the wrong word to  describe this iPhone what we actually  have here is a nearly pocketable tablet  with a killer camera a great display and  guess what it will even make some phone  calls
 

